From: SUM <sum@sexidium.local>
Date: Sat, 20 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Sexidium linearstats API delegate (L2-STATS)

Loop-2 Stage 2 (SUM): Paper-API delegate so plugins can consume Linear
stats WITHOUT net.sexidium imports.
(1) SexidiumLinearStats (io.papermc.paper.linear): public final class with
JDK-only DTO `FolderSnapshot(folderKey,folderType,worldName,reads,
readMicrosAvg,writes,writeMicrosAvg,flushes,flushMicrosAvg,
compressionLevel,filesFlushed,failures,dirtyNow)` + `snapshots()` /
`snapshot(folderKey)` delegating to the NMS coordinator
(`LinearFlushCoordinator.snapshots()` as read from minecraft-0012);
mapping converts NMS `LinearFolderSnapshot` field by field
(avg=total/count, guard divide-by-zero).
(2) LinearRegionFlushCompletedEvent (io.papermc.paper.event.linear):
ASYNC super(true) flush-granularity event with primitive-only totals
(no getTotals() NMS leak) + HandlerList + 5-line listener sample.
(3) Bridge wiring note: `SexidiumLinearFlushBridge.notifyFlush`
(from paper-0010) call-site assumed at the Paper-side save path after
`flushDirty()` (integrator to wire; the bridge takes the explicit owning
`Plugin` param — fixes the old getProvidingPlugin(Bridge.class) misuse).

BASE-TREE ASSUMPTIONS (Folia base checkout absent locally at
/tmp/sexidium-folia; all Paper hunks are written against stated assumed
context and must be re-checked by the integrator — see return message):
(C1) Coordinator method names as read from minecraft-0012: static
`LinearFlushCoordinator.snapshots()` returns
`Map<String, LinearRegionTimings.LinearFolderSnapshot>` (same key as
BY_FOLDER: absolute folder-path string); instance `snapshot()` returns
`LinearFolderSnapshot(read,write,flush,load,markDirty,filesFlushed,
failures,oversizeRejects,evicts,cacheHits,cacheMisses,dirtyDepth)` where
each timing group is `LinearTimings(count,totalMicros,maxMicros,
avgMicros)`. There is NO static `snapshot(String)` in 0012, so the
single-key `snapshot(folderKey)` here is `snapshots().get(folderKey)`
(wired explicitly; if upstream adds a direct lookup, swap to it).
(C2) Event package location: this patch places the primitive-only event at
`io.papermc.paper.event.linear` (preferred Paper-native; avoids clashing
with the paper-0010 `org.bukkit.event.world` event that carries NMS
`getTotals()`). If the target base has no `io.papermc.paper.event` tree,
relocate this file + package to `org.bukkit.event.world` (keep class name
+ primitive getters, keep super(true) + HandlerList).
(C3) compressionLevel has NO per-folder source in the coordinator snapshot
(it lives on RegionFileStorage/LinearRegionFile per 0009, clamped 1..22);
the delegate reports `compressionLevel = 0` (unknown) until a per-folder
source is wired. Do NOT fabricate a level from the timing snapshot.
(C4) Requires paper-0010 (SexidiumLinearFolderNames + bridge): folderType/
world reuse `SexidiumLinearFolderNames` (pinned region|poi|entities);
bridge wiring: `notifyFlush(Plugin,String,long,long)` ships NO call site
here — integrator must wire it into the Paper-side save path (e.g., after
`LinearFlushCoordinator.flushDirty()` in world save), passing the owning
`Plugin` explicitly (never getProvidingPlugin(Bridge.class); bridge is
server code, not a plugin jar).
(C5) dirtyNow maps to `LinearFolderSnapshot.dirtyDepth()` (int, lock-read
depth); snapshots() map keys are absolute folder-path strings.
(C6) No Bukkit lookups in NMS files (this patch is paper-side so Bukkit is
OK here; this patch adds no lookups beyond Event/HandlerList types).

